From: Developer
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] ignore freed wolfSSL sessions when updating timeouts

F-Droid's OkHttp hostnameVerifier sets SSLSessionContext.sessionTimeout
on every handshake. wolfJSSE then walks the session cache and calls
WolfSSLSession.setSessTimeout. Cached sessions whose native WOLFSSL was
already freed throw IllegalStateException, which ACRA treats as fatal.

Skip those sessions instead of aborting the handshake.

--- a/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java
+++ b/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java
@@ -552,3 +552,10 @@
     protected void setNativeTimeout(long in) {
-        ssl.setSessTimeout(in);
+        if (ssl == null) {
+            return;
+        }
+        try {
+            ssl.setSessTimeout(in);
+        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
+            /* Native WOLFSSL already freed; keep walking the session cache. */
+        }
     }
